-- title:
--   Diamond action on X_H(q²M') over X₀(q²M') for q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero. Let $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) be the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((\mathsf{q}))$ equal to the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image, under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion field $\mathbb{Q}(X_H(q^2M'))$, that is of [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101). Let $j \in K$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= \mathsf{q}^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral } j\text{-numerator series})$, and let $K_2$ be the intermediate field obtained in the same way from $\mathbb{Q}$ adjoined to the expansions $j(\mathsf{q}^d)$ for the divisors $d$ of $q^2M'$, assumed contained in $K$. Then there exist a type $G$ with a group structure, a finiteness witness for $G$, and an action of $G$ on $K$ by ring automorphisms, such that, with $K$ made a $K_2$-algebra by the inclusion, the $G$-action commutes with the $K_2$-action and $K_2 \to K$ is $G$-invariant in the sense of `Algebra.IsInvariant` (every $G$-fixed element of $K$ comes from $K_2$), the $G$-action commutes with the $L$-action, the $G$-action on $K$ is faithful, and every $g \in G$ fixes $j$.
--
--   This provides the Galois-theoretic data of the diamond operators for the covering $X_H(q^2M') \to X_0(q^2M')$, in the degenerate case $q = 2$, in the form of an unnamed finite group acting on the base-changed $q$-expansion function field with invariant subfield the $\Gamma_0$-level field and fixing the $j$-invariant. It is used in the full-level Jacobian development, where the resulting action is transported to charts and prime ideals of the associated algebras.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_mulSemiringAction_isInvariant_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_smul_j_eq_xH_of_eq_two.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_XH
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
